  "body": "Conjecture: The function open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle.recover_json_object, whose documented rule states \"The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text\", fails to distinguish two replies that the rule requires it to tell apart. Reply A is:\n~~~json\n{\"a\":1}\n~~~\n{\"b\":2}\nReply B is:\n```json\n{\"b\":2}\n```\nThe rule requires recover_json_object to return {\"a\":1} for Reply A, because the tilde fence is a code fence and the last object inside it is {\"a\":1}; and to return {\"b\":2} for Reply B, because the backtick fence holds {\"b\":2}. However, the implementation's _FENCE pattern matches only three backticks, so it ignores the tilde fence in Reply A, treats both replies as having no fenced object (or only the backtick fence in B), and returns the last top-level object {\"b\":2} for both. The observation that would show this conjecture false is if recover_json_object returns {\"a\":1} for Reply A and {\"b\":2} for Reply B, i.e., it distinguishes them as the rule requires."
